PASS 10: selected-game changes invalidate comparisons; resolution and quality A→B→A do not resurrect earlier requests
PASS 11: completed results clear on criteria/build changes, while page-local selections survive a build replacement
PASS 12: explicit limitation verified: a fresh PerformanceLab mount restores build.game defaults, not prior page-local edits
PASS 13: software/build changes reject late professional results; independent software requests survive game-only edits
PASS 14: actual request hook: latest repeated request wins, stale failures ignored, A→B→A safe, sync errors retryable, unmount blocks writes
PASS 15: catalog request cleanup suppresses state writes after unmount
PASS 16: BuildSummary loading has no fabricated option, blocks simulation, permits general summary, then enables available game
PASS 17: BuildSummary catalog errors are visible and retry recovers without a fabricated game
PASS 18: BuildSummary empty/malformed catalogs recover; missing selected game requires an available choice and retains other settings
PASS 19: BuildSummary catalog cleanup blocks post-unmount writes; incomplete build guards the simulation handler
SUMMARY: 19 scenario groups, 490 assertions passed against actual PerformanceLab/BuildSummary/useSimulationRequest source
LIMITATION: SSR and isolated handlers/hooks only; service responses are fixtures. No browser, DOM events, layout, focus, chart geometry, real network or cross-navigation persistence was tested.
NOTE: edited simulation settings are page-local; the page initializes a new mount from build.game rather than saving edits there.
